--------------------------------------------------
Table full name: isb-cgc.GDC_metadata.rel13_fileData_current
Column name: dbName Type: STRING Description: Referring to the default/main database at the GDC. In this table, this field is always current.
Column name: file_id Type: STRING Description: GDC file identifier. This is a duplicate of file_gdc_id field found in some tables. 
Column name: access Type: STRING Description: Data accessibility policy (open or controlled)
Column name: acl Type: STRING Description: Access Control List -- if access is controlled, this field contains the dbGaP accession, eg phs000179
Column name: analysis__input_files__file_id Type: STRING Description: GDC file UUIDs for input file(s)
Column name: analysis__workflow_link Type: STRING Description: Link to GDC workflow on github
Column name: analysis__workflow_type Type: STRING Description: Workflow name eg  STAR 2-Pass  
Column name: associated_entities__case_id Type: STRING Description: Associated Case ID
Column name: associated_entities__entity_id Type: STRING Description: Associated entity UUID
Column name: associated_entities__entity_submitter_id Type: STRING Description: Submitter id for associated entity(ies)
Column name: associated_entities__entity_type Type: STRING Description: Associated entity type, eg   aliquot   or   case  
Column name: cases__case_id Type: STRING Description: Associated entity case UUID
Column name: cases__project__dbgap_accession_number Type: STRING Description: DbGaP accession number for the project
Column name: cases__project__disease_type Type: STRING Description: Project Disease Type
Column name: cases__project__name Type: STRING Description: Study name of the project
Column name: cases__project__program__dbgap_accession_number Type: STRING Description: DbGaP accession number for the program
Column name: cases__project__program__name Type: STRING Description: Program Name
Column name: cases__project__project_id Type: STRING Description: Project ID
Column name: created_datetime Type: STRING Description: Timestamp of creation, eg 2016-10-27T21:58:12.297090-05:02
Column name: data_category Type: STRING Description: Category description of the underlying data, eg Clinical, Raw Sequencing Data, Simple Nucleotide Variation, Transcriptome Profiling  , etc
Column name: data_format Type: STRING Description: File format of the underlying data, eg BCR XML, BAM
Column name: data_type Type: STRING Description: File format of the underlying data, eg BCR XML, BAM
Column name: downstream_analyses__output_files__file_id Type: STRING Description: Semicolon-separated list of GDC file UUIDs
Column name: downstream_analyses__workflow_link Type: STRING Description: Name of GDC workflow, eg VarScan2 Annotation (if applicable, NULL where no information is available)
Column name: downstream_analyses__workflow_type Type: STRING Description: Name of GDC workflow, eg VarScan2 Annotation (if applicable, NULL where no information is available)
Column name: experimental_strategy Type: STRING Description: Experimental strategy used to generate data (where applicable) e.g. WXS, RNA-Seq
Column name: file_name Type: STRING Description: Name of file at the GDC
Column name: file_size Type: INT64 Description: The size of the file measured in bytes
Column name: id Type: STRING Description: GDC file identifier. This is a duplicate of file_gdc_id field found in some tables.
Column name: index_files__file_id Type: STRING Description: BAM or VCF index file GDC file UUID
Column name: index_files__file_name Type: STRING Description: BAM or VCF index file name
Column name: index_files__file_size Type: INT64 Description: BAM  or VCF index file size
Column name: md5sum Type: STRING Description: Md5sum for GDC data file
Column name: platform Type: STRING Description: Platform used to generate this data, eg  Illumina  , or  Affymetrix SNP 6.2
Column name: state Type: STRING Description: File state -- either submitted or released
Column name: submitter_id Type: STRING Description: This can be used to identify a corresponding entry in the submitter's records. The GDC requires that submitter_id be unique for each entity within a project: the tuple (combination) of [ project_id, submitter_id ] is a unique key.
Column name: type Type: STRING Description: Description of the data, e.g. clinical_supplement, aligned_reads
Column name: updated_datetime Type: STRING Description: Timestamp of latest update, eg 2017-03-04T16:37:26.081298-06:00
